---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---
<PageLayout title="Affiliate Disclosure" description="DistritoGamer may earn a commission when you buy through links on this site, at no extra cost to you. See how affiliate links work and how we stay honest." path="/affiliate-disclosure/" updated="2026-10-06"
  intro="Plain language on how DistritoGamer earns money and what that does and does not influence.">
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>{SITE.name} may earn a commission when you click certain links on this site and buy something. <strong>This does not increase the price you pay.</strong> Those commissions help fund the research and writing behind our free guides.</p>
  <h2>How we use affiliate links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Affiliate links appear only where a product recommendation is relevant to the guide, for example in an aim-training guide that discusses mouse specifications.</li>
    <li>We do not create guides just to place links.</li>
    <li>Affiliate links are marked with <code>rel="sponsored"</code>, and guides that contain buying advice carry a short disclosure near the top.</li>
    <li>Buttons that lead to a merchant are labeled plainly, such as &ldquo;Check price&rdquo;. We do not use misleading buttons or fake download links.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What affiliate relationships do not change</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>They do not decide what we recommend. We choose what to write about, and what to say about it, first.</li>
    <li>Merchants and brands do not review or approve our guides before publication.</li>
    <li>We do not invent ratings, prices, specifications, reviews or claims of hands-on testing. Where we describe gear types without testing them, the guide says so.</li>
    <li>Prices and availability change. We link to the merchant so you can see the current price rather than printing one that may be out of date.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>We may also display advertising, for example through Google AdSense, and may publish clearly labeled sponsored content in the future. Advertising is separate from editorial decisions and is shown only if you accept advertising cookies. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Programs and partners</h2>
  <p>We take part in affiliate programs only after being accepted, and we will not claim a partnership we do not have. Where an agreement requires a specific statement, it appears alongside the relevant links.</p>
  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>If anything here is unclear, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>. For how we keep editorial standards, read our <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
